unctions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type II region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $y:$\n\n$$\ny=2(x-1)^{3}+1\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y-1}{2}}+1\n$$\n\nThe function $x=0$ is already written as a function of $y.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the horizontal lines $y=1$ and $y=3.$ So, we have $1\\le y\\le 3.$\n\nWe draw a horizontal arrow through the region to determine the left function $g(y)$ and the right function $f(y).$ A horizontal line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type II region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/1dcfc91a9392998f6de0e4ede2e67d9487f71bb521adad024c3c6891b56d0163.png)\n\nThe horizontal line enters the region through the lower function $x=0$ and leaves through the upper function $x=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y-1}{2}}+1.$ So, we have $0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y-1}{2}}+1.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y-1}{2}}+1}.\n$$" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301437 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301438 13194139534650 true] [17592186301437 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301439 13194139534650 true] [17592186301437 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301440 13194139534650 true] [17592186301437 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301441 13194139534650 true] [17592186301437 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301442 13194139534650 true] [17592186301437 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534650 true] [17592186301437 1041 "selection" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301437 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301442 13194139534650 true] [17592186301437 1110 #uuid "6eaf151b-2cf1-553f-871f-64e1505e903d" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301438 1034 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2(x-1)^{3}+1,\\,1\\le x\\le 2}" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301438 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534650 true] [17592186301438 1111 #uuid "0b4bcf37-9377-578c-945a-9e418d316e9d" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301439 1034 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2(x-1)^{3}+1,\\,0\\le x\\le 1}" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301439 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534650 true] [17592186301439 1111 #uuid "ddefa05b-1d54-5f28-89b5-23a9026b2c3c" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301440 1034 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y-1}{2}}+1}" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301440 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534650 true] [17592186301440 1111 #uuid "dadb8f1f-d58a-5014-9e46-3cfe88e179a7" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301441 1034 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y-1}{2}}-1}" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301441 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534650 true] [17592186301441 1111 #uuid "1549f265-e8a4-5a1e-b8c2-5b45fb3f2cc5" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301442 1034 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y-1}{2}}+1}" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301442 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534650 true] [17592186301442 1111 #uuid "d0aa53d2-389f-5c75-90b4-2fa799a6e9da" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301443 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301444 13194139534650 true] [17592186301443 1089 "q-72185" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301443 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534650 true] [17592186301443 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region inside the circumference ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1?$\n\n- It is a type I region\n- It is a type II region\n- It's neither a type I nor a type II region" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301443 1113 #uuid "a5dd306f-63b8-5be6-adf1-ac9dc3f00602" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301443 1145 "First, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\\, & ⟹\\,x=\\pm \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\\, & ⟹\\,y=\\pm \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/0960063edcce8ccd55dc2f77147c4a4982645c180e8b998d7e520c65131ea045.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." 13194139534650 true] [17592186301444 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301445 13194139534650 true] [17592186301444 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301446 13194139534650 true] [17592186301444 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301447 13194139534650 true] [17592186301444 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301448 13194139534650 true] [17592186301444 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301449 13194139534650 true] [17592186301444 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534650 true] [17592186301444 1041 "selection" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301444 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301448 13194139534650 true] [17592186301444 1110 #uuid "a2ceb530-70bd-5b73-b3ec-0ae8db0a36f7" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301445 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301445 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534650 true] [17592186301445 1111 #uuid "1a0f3222-a5f8-5fcd-b098-fcccf3105990" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301446 1034 "I only" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301446 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534650 true] [17592186301446 1111 #uuid "4efd1cc1-35fd-5180-98b1-c020add13878" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301447 1034 "III only" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301447 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534650 true] [17592186301447 1111 #uuid "fc67656a-c62a-5f24-8999-265587a5d457" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301448 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301448 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534650 true] [17592186301448 1111 #uuid "12f729bd-320f-50de-bd74-5b2cd483e355" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301449 1034 "II only" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301449 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534650 true] [17592186301449 1111 #uuid "81814992-97d4-5d06-b32c-f9c0ba5e739c" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301450 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301451 13194139534650 true] [17592186301450 1089 "q-72186" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301450 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534650 true] [17592186301450 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the parabola $y=4-{x}^{2}$ and the line $y=2-|x|?$\n\n- It is a type I region\n- It is a type II region\n- It's neither a type I nor a type II region" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301450 1113 #uuid "ab932e6b-af0e-5e9b-9cca-659edaed65a4" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301450 1145 "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/6f35161e7efbd53c9ef558ffe88d8e046771128965a9fdd02143ae37a9b130ea.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,2-|x|\\le y\\le 4-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- The horizontal line $y=1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/769a521cd6b05ecf05052da382e40295b26be66fe56e4eff7c6940c9032f2f0b.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." 13194139534650 true] [17592186301451 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301452 13194139534650 true] [17592186301451 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301453 13194139534650 true] [17592186301451 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301454 13194139534650 true] [17592186301451 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301455 13194139534650 true] [17592186301451 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301456 13194139534650 true] [17592186301451 1040 #edb/ref 1759218