pe II region is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/1206abdf317df09c8c54714a6178d78570b3c10a49513c3c626c09be3ea2cf72.png)" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301458 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301459 13194139534650 true] [17592186301458 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301460 13194139534650 true] [17592186301458 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301461 13194139534650 true] [17592186301458 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301462 13194139534650 true] [17592186301458 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301463 13194139534650 true] [17592186301458 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534650 true] [17592186301458 1041 "selection" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301458 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301463 13194139534650 true] [17592186301458 1110 #uuid "ffde4384-1824-5572-92af-e06b7dba1323" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301459 1034 "None of the listed" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301459 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534650 true] [17592186301459 1111 #uuid "eb4569cc-7afa-5db6-abb8-57be792aa56e" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301460 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/3228d2d0c2fb3ce74c98b018c0694e9da5fc4a8444a7b67b5fb7fa0eb24eaa6c.png" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301460 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534650 true] [17592186301460 1111 #uuid "619bee74-f842-5275-9ba5-56fcecc92ace" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301461 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/ef9d0a612a093852fd9f60fb20c86b946c178f9e2a9877ef7c16f89f98e324f6.png" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301461 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534650 true] [17592186301461 1111 #uuid "0f6b6ea4-a669-5de2-90da-f16756eaf873" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301462 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/67b42d8a49263abc8cce98f20b59370047b989ae69d55050e4001897ba3f9d2e.png" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301462 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534650 true] [17592186301462 1111 #uuid "c8bf809a-76e2-5a32-bbe4-71a057091fb0" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301463 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/5eb14fb126d8b0df54e5523d705cb5491e161c00b118f07a0bf3407644b7d4a0.png" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301463 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534650 true] [17592186301463 1111 #uuid "8908f108-2e4e-58f2-80c4-dece6295a81e" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301464 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301465 13194139534650 true] [17592186301464 1089 "q-73532" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301464 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534650 true] [17592186301464 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/d69e6b6550f7e4cae0785daaa19c0a52382a595c40309dccd1d832dbc6d2f82f.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type I region in two-dimensional space?" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301464 1113 #uuid "5386da7a-d4e3-5516-bd15-c0227ea4ae2c" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301464 1145 "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type I region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $x:$\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{y-1}+1\\,⟹\\,y=(x-1)^{2}+1\n$$\n\nThe function $y=-(x-1)^{2}+3$ is already written as a function of $x.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the vertical lines $x=1$ and $x=2.$ So, we have $1\\le x\\le 2.$\n\nWe draw a vertical arrow through the region to determine the lower function $g(x)$ and the upper function $f(x).$ A vertical line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type I region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/942a39f885e6f88bef997e27914d05359be86ae1d6204f3834f0829ce4b81136.png)\n\nThe vertical line enters the region through the lower function $y=(x-1)^{2}+1$ and leaves through the upper function $y=-(x-1)^{2}+3.$ So, we have $(x-1)^{2}+1\\le y\\le -(x-1)^{2}+3.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,(x-1)^{2}+1\\le y\\le -(x-1)^{2}+3}.\n$$" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301465 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301466 13194139534650 true] [17592186301465 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301467 13194139534650 true] [17592186301465 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301468 13194139534650 true] [17592186301465 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301469 13194139534650 true] [17592186301465 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301470 13194139534650 true] [17592186301465 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534650 true] [17592186301465 1041 "selection" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301465 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301468 13194139534650 true] [17592186301465 1110 #uuid "22c2f92c-84cf-5c4e-8386-899599683563" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301466 1034 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-{x}^{2}+3\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+1}" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301466 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534650 true] [17592186301466 1111 #uuid "9b882010-5288-5d0a-bbff-29b6ad594ed7" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301467 1034 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le -(x-1)^{2}+3}" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301467 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534650 true] [17592186301467 1111 #uuid "c19dd8db-321b-5a04-8a6d-2464c52803a1" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301468 1034 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,(x-1)^{2}+1\\le y\\le -(x-1)^{2}+3}" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301468 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534650 true] [17592186301468 1111 #uuid "62a50ee6-80f9-5e55-8bbd-05a650d8c085" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301469 1034 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,(x-1)^{2}+3\\le y\\le -(x-1)^{2}+1}" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301469 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534650 true] [17592186301469 1111 #uuid "7b920f50-2ccc-5392-922a-1341e3c1bdf4" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301470 1034 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le -(x-1)^{2}}" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301470 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534650 true] [17592186301470 1111 #uuid "8c1bdea2-0bb8-5bb6-ae9e-62a3e14c8638" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301471 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301472 13194139534650 true] [17592186301471 1089 "q-73552" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301471 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534650 true] [17592186301471 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the ellipses $(x-1)^{2}+4{y}^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=4?$\n\n- It is a type I region\n- It is a type II region\n- It's neither a type I nor a type II region" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301471 1113 #uuid "964e90c7-3ddc-59ef-9c19-6cc6da31e561" 13194139534650 true] [17592186301471 1145 "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/215dd0c920e700a75896fc54751ec20d197487a2c992cd8910810c66129c14dc.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/7e1a0c5dd2b4aadf7efe78d903234b8d00cf4fa92eb7a3b41209a856f2d14b01.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=0.25$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/a90d7306e3f88a31609e368f9362248d6a12b7922b6a9e8c9f980ab31e7fb140.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." 13194139534650 true] [17592186301472 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301473 13194139534650 true] [17592186301472 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301474 13194139534650 true] [175